WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.402
-We don't always have
enough time

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.004
to cover everything
in the recent news,

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:08.274
so here with a recap is one of
our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.977
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.212 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.080
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.315
-You guys!

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.684
Things have been crazy.
Okay.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:22.355
First of all, Nike came out
with a Colin Kaepernick ad,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.791
and everyone was like, "What?"

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.525
Only some people were like,
"What?"

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:29.128
And some people were like,
"What?"

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.130
And I was like, "What, what?"

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.535
Then Nike ran that ad
during Thursday Night Football,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.538
and I was like
[Laughing] "Oh, what?!"

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.207
It was such a kick in the nuts
to racists,

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.076
they're gonna have to take
a knee.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.244
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.714
Then -- Then Aretha Franklin's
funeral happened,

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.316
and it was amazing.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.451
First, and this is true,

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.054
Aretha had
four different outfit changes

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.889
at her own funeral!

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.924
I was like, "What?!"

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.127
Then, more than 100
pink Cadillacs

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.929
escorted her hearse
into the funeral,

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.430
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.467
Then, Fantasia sang,
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.770
And then she took her shoes off,
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.638
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.808
Then I looked down,
and she had sung my shoes off,

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.344
and I was like, "Well, what?"

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.713
Then, they were like,
"Next up is Faith Hill,"

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.381
and I was like,
"Yay, Faith Hill!"

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.984
And then she came on,
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.387
That's when I learned Faith Hill
is not Faith Evans,

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:31.291
and in my mind,
they were both Faith Evans,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.692
and now I understand
why Faith Evans

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.361
won best country album --

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.930
because she did not.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.931
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.734
Then, after Ariana Grande sang,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.837
some creepy pastor grabbed
some serious side boob,

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:48.107
and I was like, "What...
do you think you're doing?"

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.043
Do you think we cannot see you?"

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:53.079
Then he made a joke about her
name being off a Taco Bell menu,

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:57.784
and I was like, "What...
has happened to your brain?

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.385
Did the energy from her boob

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.988
suck the common sense
out of your head?"

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.391
Oh, it made me so mad!
I was like, "What?"

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.660
Then, I saw some big,
fancy bunch of fabric,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.328
and I was like,
"Ooh! What's this?"

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.397
And I looked under it
and found Cicely Tyson,

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.033
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.570
She looked so perfect,
I could not handle it.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.206
Then, two days later,
the funeral was over.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:24.144
Then, Fox News posted a story

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.112
trying to shame
actor Geoffrey Owens

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.814
for working at a Trader Joe's,
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:32.418
I didn't know you could
be shamed for having a job.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.120
Just because he was on a sitcom
does not mean he's rich.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.123
People on TV don't make
what you think.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.659
Seth asked me to borrow $10
this morning.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.062
-What?
I did not!

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.698
-Then,
something insane happened --

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.234
the president
of the French Tennis Federation

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.304
said Serena's French Open
catsuit went too far,

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.905
and I was like, "Quoi?"

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:56.075
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.612
In a sport where this, this,
and this

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.882
are regular things to wear,
this is too far?

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.885
Maybe the thing you have
a problem with is her body.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.654
And I know a lot of people
aren't ready to hear this part,

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.656
but when you're skinny,
people let you live.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.291
But when you're a curvaceous
black woman,

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.627
people feel like it's okay
to tell you to cover up.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.063
I tell you what.
-Whoo!

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.464
-Goddamn right, "Whoo!"

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.966
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.168
I tell you what,
if I had Serena's body,

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.936
you couldn't get no clothes
on me.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.104
I'd be too beautiful
and too fast!

00:03:26.104 --> 00:03:28.141
[ Cheers and applause]

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.945
Aah!

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.649
Then, during Saturday's
championship,

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.384
things got crazy.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:42.188
For the first time in history,
a tennis player got frustrated.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.323
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.392
And it warranted
a loss of a point,

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.128
a loss of a game,
and a racist cartoon.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:52.765
I saw that and was like,
"What else is new?"

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.634
And I know a lot of you aren't
ready to hear this, but...

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.803
when you're a white man,

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.804
your whole tennis career
can be about tantrums.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.239
But when you're a black woman,

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.241
that same behavior
will cost you dearly.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:05.078
Afterwards, in an interview,
Serena said...

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:18.891
That's class!

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.761
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ser -- Ooh!

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.763
Yeah!

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.898
I love her. I love her.
I love her so bad.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:29.836
Serena Williams makes me want
to be a better person,

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.605
but not right now
because now,

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.807
some tennis umpires
are reportedly thinking

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.009
about boycotting Serena's games.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.477
Well, guess what?

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:41.613
Tennis doesn't belong to you,
you raggedy pieces of [bleep]

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:43.816
It's not her fault
she dominates a sport

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.918
you so desperately want
to keep white!

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.454
She's excellent!
Too [bleep] bad!

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:52.124
And it's the referee's fault she
yelled, not hers!

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:53.592
Asking her to shut up
and take it

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:55.761
is asking her to be complicit
in her own abuse,

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.430
and we don't do that anymore.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.698
But...

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.733
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:05.672
I don't know if people
are ready to hear that yet.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.739
[ Ting! ]

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.107
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.575
Then I found out
people are saying

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.645
that Prime Minister
Theresa May's Brexit strategy

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.213
means disaster for Britain.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:18.550
And I was like,
"What...is that jacket?"

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.219
Where did you get it from?

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:22.854
I would wear the ass
off that jacket!

00:05:22.854 --> 00:05:24.257
Would it look good on me?

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.092
Could I ask
the graphics department?

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:29.162
Ooh.
That's nice.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.263
Do I dress like Theresa May?

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.232
I guess I do.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:36.368
Then, something that makes
less than no sense happened.

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:40.105
Okay. I found out Putin
has appointed Steven Seagal

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:43.542
the new Russian ministry
special representative,

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.312
and I was like, "Why?!"

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:49.582
Which brings us to a new segment
called "Amber Says Why."

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.017
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:55.821
Putin, you want to improve
relations with America,

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:59.124
and you picked Steven Seagal?

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:00.926
Why?

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:02.328
Why did you do this,

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.063
and what exactly is
what you did?

00:06:05.063 --> 00:06:06.231
What is it for?

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.601
Fun? Nothing? What?

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.935
Who gets something from it,

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:12.337
and why do they get
what they get?

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:15.507
And what is what they get?

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.844
Why do you?
Why did you?

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.012
Why did you do what you do?

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.715
Also, is this
the kind of thing you do,

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:25.084
and where is this, exactly?

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:27.820
Where does it take place,
and for whom?

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.222
Who can see it
when it is happening,

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:33.392
and who are they
and why are they that?

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:35.594
And what will this do?

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:39.098
And are you sure you want
what this will do did?

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:42.401
Also, do you know
who Steven Seagal is,

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:44.036
or, much more likely,

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:47.139
do you think he is someone
he is not?

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.375
Who do you think he is?

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.009
Can you see him?

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:53.512
When you look at him,
what do you see?

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:55.114
Something good?

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:58.583
In closing, why?

00:06:58.583 --> 00:07:01.453
This has been "Amber Says What
&amp; Then She Says Why."

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:03.255
♪♪

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.090
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.028
-Give it up
for Amber Ruffin, everybody!

